      "writtenOn": "2022-03-24T20:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is more like `unapplyBitNot` than anything, since it only returns a real Val if the instruction contains a bit-not. I changed it to `holdsBitNot` so that it looks less like a boolean return (although it still does a little, but I don\u0027t know how to convey \"retrieve the original Val iff this points to a bit-not\" succinctly enough)",
      "parentUuid": "18b30806_c9ec9c1d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1020,
